# Building documentation

Run these commands from the repository root:

- `just docs::make` (or `just docs::zensical`) builds the Zensical site
  in `docs/build/zensical`, staging Markdown and API pages in `docs/build/markdown`.
- `just docs::clean` (or `just docs::zensical-clean`) removes the generated site
  and staged Markdown.

From this directory, omit the `docs::` prefix. The build commands accept extra
arguments for Zensical.

Zensical uses `zensical.toml`, the top-level Markdown files, `_static`, `overrides`,
and `scripts`. Legacy Sphinx content is archived in `sphinx` and is not built.
